  "sticker": "beaver",
  "skeleton": "sitting beaver, three-quarter view facing left: root at the seat; body with belly squash; head on the body, face with eyes and mouth (big front teeth); armL/armR at the shoulders holding the stick (a separate prop on its own bone in the paws); footL/footR on the root; flat tail at the rump (slaps).",
  "sheets": [
    {
      "id": "parts",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a beaver character holding a little stick. Draw this exact beaver as a cut-out paper puppet: its separate body parts laid out on one sheet, the same drawing style, colours, texture, line and proportions as in image 1, every part at the size it has in image 1.\n\nDraw each part on its own, spread out over the sheet with wide empty gaps between them, no part touching or overlapping another:\n1. the body: the plump brown sitting body with its cream tummy, without head, arms, feet or tail; its top, normally under the head, rounded.\n2. the head: the round brown head with its two small round ears, whiskers and nose, facing left as in image 1, with a completely blank face — no eyes, no mouth, no teeth — keep the nose, the whiskers and the rosy cheeks; its bottom edge rounded.\n3. one arm: the arm on the right of image 1, bent, its paw closed as if holding something, with a rounded shoulder.\n4. the stick: the little gnawed stick with its two green leaves, on its own.\n5. one foot: a big dark webbed hind foot, as in image 1.\n6. the tail: the flat dark brown paddle tail with its criss-cross pattern, with a rounded base.\n\nEvery part is drawn whole, including what is normally hidden behind another part, and each joint end (where it tucks under the body or the head) is a full, smooth, rounded edge. No text, no labels, no numbers, no outline around the parts beyond the drawing's own line, no shadows. Fully transparent background."
    },
    {
      "id": "face",
      "size": "1536x1024",
      "references": [
        "parts"
      ],
      "prompt": "Image 1 is a sticker of a beaver character holding a little stick; image 2 shows the same beaver cut into puppet parts, with a blank face. Draw the beaver's face pieces as separate stickers on one sheet: the same drawing style, colours and line as in image 1, every piece at the size it has on the beaver in image 1, so it fits the blank face in image 2.\n\nDraw each piece on its own, spread out in tidy rows with wide empty gaps between them, nothing touching:\n1. the beaver's left eye (on the right of image 1) as it is in image 1: a dark round eye with a white sparkle.\n2. the same eye wide open and surprised: bigger and rounder, with its white sparkle.\n3. the same eye gently closed in sleep: a soft downward-curving line with a few lashes.\n4. the same eye closed in a happy smile: an upward-curving arc.\n5. the same eye sad: looking down, its upper lid tilted up towards the middle.\n6. the mouth as it is in image 1: a happy smile showing two big front teeth.\n7. the mouth with the two big front teeth biting, gnawing.\n8. the mouth wide open in a big happy laugh, the inside pink.\n9. the mouth open in a small round 'o'.\n10. the mouth in a small sad frown.\n\nNo text, no labels, no numbers, no shadows, no face or head around the pieces. Fully transparent background."
    }
